From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wangzlei <66336933+wangzlei@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:38:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] forwarded-host: X-Forwarded-Host / Host on server spans
 and HTTP server RED

Record the front-door name an incoming HTTP request was addressed to: the
X-Forwarded-Host request header, or the Host header when X-Forwarded-Host is
absent. It is exported as the x-forwarded-host attribute on server spans, and
(first entry, without the port) as peer.service.name on the HTTP server RED
metrics (http.server.request.duration / request.body.size / response.body.size).

Why: behind an L7 load balancer (e.g. ALB) the TCP-option service name
(patch 01/03) cannot cross the hop, so the caller side loses peer.service.name.
The request headers still carry the name the client used. Upstream OBI only
uses Host for the span's Statement field and never reads X-Forwarded-Host.

Paths: kprobe HTTP/1.x legacy buffer (header scan of the captured request,
case-insensitive, truncated values ignored), kprobe large-buffer path
(req.Header / req.Host) and the Go uprobe tracer (req.Host only). RPC/DB server
metrics keep the shared serverInfo group unchanged.

Adot-Obi-Patch: 04-forwarded-host
